cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "beam-opt-framework: size optimisation of curved 3-D beam structures"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pezone
    given-names: Benito
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/benitopezone-creator/beam-opt-framework"
keywords:
  - structural optimization
  - size optimization
  - curved beams
  - finite element method
  - ANSYS MAPDL
  - APDL
abstract: >-
  Python framework for the size optimisation of curved three-dimensional beam
  structures. The cross-section dimensions vary along the arc length and are
  optimised for minimum mass under stress, stiffness and reaction-force
  constraints, with a built-in beam solver or ANSYS MAPDL, selectable
  optimisation algorithms and APDL import/export.
